From: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp@gmail.com>
Subject: econet-eth: only bind/scan on HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED (fix CPU saturation)

After egress was moved to hardware (crsn 0x16 gone, bound flows bypass the
CPU) throughput was still ~3 Mbit with the CPU pinned at 0% idle / 33% sirq.
Cause: the RX commit path runs a full 16384-entry FOE table scan to find the
engine's learned slot, and it ran for every UN_HIT/HIT_UNBIND packet of every
not-yet-bound flow (~200/s), each scan reading the whole table uncached under
spin_lock_irqsave - ~0.7s of CPU per second, collapsing throughput.

The engine emits HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED (0x0f) precisely when a flow is hot
enough to bind, and at that moment its UNBIND entry was just hit so it is
guaranteed present - the scan finds it on the first try and the flow binds once,
then stays COMMITTED and is forwarded in hardware. Trigger the commit only on
0x0f; leave 0x0d/0x0e on the normal slow path. This drops the scan rate from
per-packet to roughly once per hot flow.

diff -ruN b130/econet_qdma.c b131/econet_qdma.c
--- a/econet_qdma.c	2026-06-29 22:28:50.170190374 +0300
+++ b/econet_qdma.c	2026-06-29 22:29:03.233506231 +0300
@@ -224,10 +224,13 @@
 	}
 
 	switch (get_erx_crsn(&desc.msg.erx)) {
-	case 0x0d:	/* UN_HIT: under FORWARD the hardware reports the real
-			 * hash slot on a miss; publish any staged entry. */
-	case 0x0e:	/* HIT_UNBIND */
-	case 0x0f:	/* HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED */
+	case 0x0f:	/* HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED: the engine just hit an UNBIND
+			 * entry often enough to ask us to bind it. Only act here:
+			 * the UNBIND entry is guaranteed present (it was just hit)
+			 * so the table scan finds it first try, and this fires
+			 * roughly once per hot flow instead of on every miss -
+			 * the per-packet scan was saturating the CPU. Plain
+			 * UN_HIT/HIT_UNBIND (0x0d/0x0e) are left on the slow path. */
 		en75_ppe_offload_rx_commit(en75_eth_ppe(q->qdma->eth), skb, hash);
 		break;
 	case 0x16: {	/* HIT_BIND_FORCE_CPU: a bound entry was hit. Log once
